#: includes/class-abilities.php:196
msgid "List content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:197
msgid "Search and paginate posts in a REST-enabled post type, most recently modified first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:204
msgid "Only this status. Default: every status except trash."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:209
msgid "Sort field. Default modified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:214
msgid "Sort direction. Default desc (asc for title)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:230
msgid "Read content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:231
msgid "Read a post by ID, URL or slug: raw Gutenberg markup, terms, featured image, SEO meta, the builder that stores its layout, your autosave if any, and the content hash needed for updates. Pass autosave_content to read the text of your staged autosave."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:236
msgid "Permalink of the post, as an alternative to post_id."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:237
msgid "Post slug, as an alternative to post_id. Combine with post_type for pages or custom types."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:239
msgid "Also return the title, content and excerpt of your autosave. Edits to live posts are staged there, so read it back after such a save."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:246
msgid "Save content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:247
msgid "Create a draft or update a post through WordPress. Updates need the current content hash from get-content. Edits to a published, private or scheduled post are saved as your autosave for review unless you pass status (for example publish) to change the live post. Publishing or scheduling always requires status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:251
msgid "Post to update. Omit to create a post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:252
msgid "Post type for a new post. Default post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:253
msgid "Plain-text title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:254
msgid "Complete post content, usually serialized Gutenberg block markup. Replaces the existing content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:255
msgid "Manual excerpt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:258
msgid "New status. Omit to keep drafts as drafts and stage edits to live posts. future needs a future date_gmt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:261
msgid "URL slug. WordPress makes it unique."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:262
msgid "Publish date in UTC, ISO 8601, for example 2026-10-05T09:00:00Z. A future date with status publish or future schedules the post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:265
msgid "Replace terms per taxonomy, for example {\"category\": [3], \"post_tag\": [\"seo\", 12]}. Integers are term IDs; strings are names, created when missing. Use list-terms to find IDs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:275
msgid "Image attachment ID for the featured image, or 0 to remove it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:278
msgid "Post meta to set, for example SEO title and description fields. Only keys listed in get-content meta support are accepted; an empty string deletes the value."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:284
msgid "content_sha256 from get-content. Required for updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:291
msgid "List terms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:292
msgid "Find categories, tags or other taxonomy terms and their IDs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:296
msgid "REST-enabled taxonomy such as category or post_tag. Default category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:309
msgid "List media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:310
msgid "Find existing media library items with their URLs, alt text and dimensions. Prefer existing media over new uploads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:314
msgid "Filter by MIME type or family, for example image or image/png."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:327
msgid "List skills"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:328
msgid "List bundled builder and plugin skills, plus skills active plugins add. Includes MailerHive, Core Support, FluentCart, GT Extensions for FluentCart, Stackless and Page Blocks Builder (PBB), with installed versions, whether each is active and its files. Read the matching skill before layout or plugin work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:354
msgid "Read skill"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:355
msgid "Read a skill from list-skills: a bundled builder or plugin skill, or one an active plugin adds. Start with its SKILL.md, which explains the workflow and which reference files to read next."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:359
msgid "Skill name from list-skills."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:360
msgid "File within the skill, for example references/elements.md. Default SKILL.md."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:375
msgid "List Bricks abilities"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:376
msgid "List Bricks Builder's own abilities on this site: name, label, one-line summary, readonly and destructive hints, and the tool name of those also served directly (bricks-*). Pass ability_name for the full description and the input and output schemas. Use this where Bricks guidance names mcp-adapter-discover-abilities or mcp-adapter-get-ability-info."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:380
msgid "A Bricks ability, for example bricks/get-page-elements, to return in full with its schemas."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:381
msgid "Only list abilities whose name, label or description contains this text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:408
msgid "Run Bricks ability"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:409
msgid "Run one of Bricks Builder's own abilities with its parameters. Use this where Bricks guidance names mcp-adapter-execute-ability; ability_name and parameters work the same way. Bricks checks its own permissions and validates the parameters against the ability's input schema. Abilities that are not readonly change the site: follow Bricks' readback and revision guidance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:413
msgid "Bricks ability name from bricks-abilities, for example bricks/get-page-elements."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:414
msgid "The ability's input, matching its input schema. Omit for abilities that take no input."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:427
msgid "Upload media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:428
msgid "Import a file into the media library from a public URL or base64 data, with alt text. WordPress checks the file type. Use the returned ID as featured_media or the URL in content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:432
msgid "Public http(s) URL to import. Private and loopback addresses are refused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:433
