#: includes/class-admin.php:111
msgid "Enable Site Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:111
msgid "Allow authenticated administrators to connect and use the tools selected below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:112
msgid "URL authentication"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:112
msgid "Not recommended. Allow Base64-encoded username and Application Password credentials in the MCP endpoint auth query parameter. The password is only encoded, and URLs can be recorded in client history, chats and server logs. Use OAuth connections instead whenever the client supports them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:113
msgid "OAuth connections (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:113
msgid "On by default. Let MCP clients that support OAuth, such as Claude and ChatGPT connectors, connect by signing in here. An administrator approves each client on a consent screen and picks its tool groups. Clients get one-hour access tokens and refresh tokens that end after 30 days without use. No password is shared with the client."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:114
msgid "Content writes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:114
msgid "Create drafts, edit posts or pages, set terms, featured images and SEO fields, and import media. Edits to live posts are staged as autosaves unless a status is passed explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:115
msgid "Source inspection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:115
msgid "Read plugin, theme and must-use plugin source files. Source files can contain sensitive data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:116
msgid "Source editing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:116
msgid "Create, overwrite, move or delete plugin and theme files, including PHP. PHP changes that cause a fatal error are reverted when the site can be checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:117
msgid "PHP execution"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:117
msgid "Run PHP inside WordPress with the server process privileges. This is not a sandbox and can modify files, the database, and Site Agent itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:118
msgid "WP-CLI execution"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:119
msgid "Bricks tools"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:119
msgid "Serve Bricks Builder's own abilities (Bricks 2.4 or later, with AI/MCP enabled in Bricks > Settings > AI): its fast-path tools directly and the rest through one dispatcher. They can change pages, templates, global classes, variables, theme styles and Bricks settings. Bricks' own switches and permission checks still apply, and its PHP ability also needs PHP execution."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:120
msgid "Audit history"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:120
msgid "Keep the last 100 tool calls: time, user ID, tool, target (post ID, file path or WP-CLI command name), Application Password name, result and duration. Content, code, other arguments, outputs, IP addresses and credential secrets are not logged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:121
msgid "Delete data on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:121
msgid "Remove Site Agent settings, password limits, audit history and the update license when deleting the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:127
msgid "Site Agent requires site administration rights, or super administrator rights on multisite."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:143
msgid "Connect your AI client directly to this WordPress installation. Site Agent has no hosted proxy and makes no telemetry requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:145
msgid "SITE_AGENT_DISABLED is active. All Site Agent access is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:148
msgid "WordPress file modification or editing is disabled. Source inspection, source editing, PHP, and WP-CLI tools are blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:151
msgid "SITE_AGENT_ALLOW_EXECUTION is false in wp-config.php. Source editing, PHP, and WP-CLI tools are blocked on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:162
msgid "Unavailable: Bricks abilities are not active. They need the Bricks theme 2.4 or later with AI/MCP enabled in Bricks > Settings > AI."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:164
